Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 50 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer metastatic to axillary lymph nodes  She was treated with preoperative chemotherapy and now undergoes left breast needle localization lumpectomy with axillary dissection  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The breast tissue was extensively sampled  The absence of tumor in the specimen likely reflects preoperative chemotherapy  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CEPHALAD MARGIN   EXCISION  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple levels were examined  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CAUDAD MARGIN   EXCISION  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA PRESENT IN TWO OF EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES  2 18    SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   1  SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  INCLUDING SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  18  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  NOTE  The metastatic tumor cells are present in association with sclerosis  likely due to prior treatment effect  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm unoriented portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan white  ill defined  soft to firm and focally cystic irregular mass which grossly abuts the overlying inked margin  The adjacent breast parenchyma shows foci of fat necrosis  The metallic clip is not grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  mass to overlying inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  breast parenchyma  away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Opposite margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of breast parenchyma Received are four containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast cephalad final margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast caudad final margin   is an unoriented  irregular portion of yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast medial final margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final lateral margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary nodes  contents    is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  which is dissected and palpated to reveal 19 possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  All candidate nodes are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing one possible node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible nodes  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible nodes  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing four possible nodes  submitted entirely  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CEPHALAD MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CAUDAD MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  report_end  , 0.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  16 MAY 98 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  Right mastectomy with TRAM                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1 RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   2 ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3 METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 19 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite stromal blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of carcinoma  The metastatic carcinoma consists of small clusters of cells in the subcapsular sinus of two nodes  the metastatic cells are keratin positive  BREAST   RIGHT BREAST FLAP    BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  21 MAY 98 at 17 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 23 x 16 x 6 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying 22 x 10 5cm skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  and a 6 0cm linear scar located in the lateral upper quadrant  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail is also attached to the specimen  The anterior superior surface is inked blue  the anterior inferior surface is inked green  and the deep resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm cavity filled with brown red hematoma surrounded by indurated  fibrotic parenchyma  abutting the closest deep resection margin  and 2 5cm from the closest anterior superior and 2 5cm from the closest anterior inferior resection margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Section code  A  biopsy cavity and adjacent closest deep resection margin  B F  representative sections of the indurated wall of the biopsy cavity  G I  representative sections of the breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity  J N  representative sections of the axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue fragments  One fragment is attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm grossly unremarkable tan skin ellipse  Serial sectioning of the specimen reveals no gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in cassette O  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  FLAP   RESECTION   report_end  , 2.
